  font-size:var(--t-h3);line-height:1.42;font-weight:400;color:var(--graphite);max-width:44ch}
#v-ent #en-build .join b{font-weight:400;color:var(--ink)}

/* ---------- closing ---------- */
/* The closing block used to stop dead on Jet against the Paper footer, which
   read as a slide edge. It now descends into Jet and climbs back out the same
   way, so the page ends on the ground it started on -- the same shape the
   Cart recovery and landing closings already use. The bloom moved off the
   bottom edge (118%) to sit behind the copy, where it no longer tints the
   Pale band on the way back up. */
/* The closing block sat as a dark slab between the light preset wall and the
   light footer, which is what read as a slide however smooth its edges were.
   It is now the same light field, in the shape the Cart recovery closing
   already uses -- Paper in, Pale through the middle, Paper out -- so the whole
   back half of the page is one continuous ground and the only transition left
   on the page is the one out of the hero. */
#v-ent #en-cta{overflow:hidden;color:var(--ink);background:
  radial-gradient(78% 52% at 50% 52%, rgba(49,92,255,.16) 0%, rgba(49,92,255,.06) 48%, rgba(0,0,0,0) 76%),
  linear-gradient(180deg,#F4F1E8 0%,#E8EDFF 44%,#E8EDFF 60%,#F4F1E8 100%)}
#v-ent #en-cta .in{width:100%;text-align:center;max-width:calc(var(--content) + var(--pad-x)*2);
  margin-inline:auto;padding:clamp(124px,13vw,190px) var(--pad-x) clamp(124px,13vw,190px)}
#v-ent #en-cta h2{color:var(--ink);font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,72px);line-height:1.06;
  letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:0 auto 22px;max-width:18ch;text-wrap:balance}
#v-ent #en-cta .lede{color:var(--graphite);margin:0 auto clamp(34px,4vw,48px);max-width:60ch;
  text-align:center;text-wrap:balance}
#v-ent #en-cta .ctas{display:flex;gap:12px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}

